If a clinician works in a practice-context and a virtual-visit is a standard-care in the practice-context and an observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment is available then the clinician may conduct the observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment with a patient.
If a patient has an in-person-follow-up-visit-challenge and an observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment is available then every clinician may conduct the observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment with the patient.
If a clinician conducts an observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment with a patient then the clinician can communicate with the patient through the observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment and can observe the patient through the observational-telehealth-follow-up-assessment.
A virtual-visit-standard-care-practice-context-example is a distance-or-other-context-challenged-remote-area-example.
An in-person-follow-up-visit-challenge-example is a frail-patient-example.
